  "body_markdown": "About us\n\nmeet Dr. ChrisMeet The TeamLivewell DifferenceOffice TourTechnologyJoin Our Team\n\nservices\n\ndCOEFull Mouth ReconstructionSedation Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nSmile MakeoverPorcelain VeneersNo Prep VeneersGum RecontouringTeeth WhiteningDental Bonding\n\nImplant Dentistry\n\nDental ImplantsSingle ImplantsImplant BridgesAll-on-X ImplantsLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nDental CrownsInlays & OnlaysDental BridgesTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone GraftingRidge AugmentationTooth ExtractionSinus LiftWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nOrthodontics\n\nInvisalignBraces\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPreventive DentistryPreventive CleaningGum TherapyRoot Canal Therapy\n\nTMJ TreatmentDental Emergencies\n\nnew patient\n\nfirst visit & new examInsurance & FinancingBlog\n\nOur work\n\nSmile GalleryTestimonials\n\nContact\n\ncall (703) 690-0102Request An Appointment\n\nBook Now\n\n703-690-0102\n\nLivewell Difference\n\nmeet Dr. Chris\n\nMeet The Team\n\nJoin Our Team\n\nOffice Tour\n\nTechnology\n\nServices\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nDCOE\n\nTMJ Treatment\n\nDental Emergencies\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPreventive\n\nDental Bridges\n\nRoot Canal\n\nProfessional Dental Cleaning\n\nScaling & Root Planing\n\nAll General Dentistry services\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nNo Prep Veneers\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nGum Recontouring\n\nAll Cosmetic Dentistry Services\n\nSingle Implants\n\nImplant Bridges\n\nAll-on-X Implants\n\nLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nAll Implant Dentistry Services\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nTooth Extraction\n\nSinus Lift\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nInvisalign\n\nBraces\n\nAll Orthodontics Services\n\nDental Crowns\n\nTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nDental Bonding\n\nInlays & Onlays\n\nAll Restorative Dentistry Services\n\nNew Patient\n\nfirst visit & new exam\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nBlog\n\nTestimonials\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nCALL US: (703) 690-0102\n\nBOOK AN APPOINTMENT\n\n320+\n\n5 Star Reviews\n\n\n# Invisalign in Fairfax Station, VA\n\n\nClear aligners, no brackets or wires\n\nPlanned by Dr. Chris, start to finish\n\nDigital preview before treatment begins\n\n\n## Most People Wait Too Long to Fix This\n\n\nYou've thought about it. Crowded teeth, a gap you've learned to hide, a bite that never felt quite right.\n\nCrooked or crowded teeth - wearing unevenly, harder to keep clean\n\nGaps or spacing - affecting how your bite closes and how your smile looks\n\nBite misalignment - overbite, underbite, or crossbite creating long-term wear\n\nThese aren't just cosmetic problems. Left alone, they can compound, and fixing them later may require more than aligners.\n\n\n## What Is Invisalign?\n\n\nInvisalign is a series of custom clear aligners that move your teeth in small, controlled steps. You wear each set for one to two weeks, then advance to the next. No brackets, no wires, nothing cemented to your teeth.\n\nWhat most people don't realize: the aligner brand isn't what determines the result. Case planning does.\n\n\n## We Ask What's Causing This Before We Discuss What to Fix\n\n\nStart With a Consultation\n\nMost offices take a scan, show you a simulation, and hand you aligners. We slow down before that step. Orthodontic problems often have an underlying cause - a bite that's off, crowding driven by jaw structure, or wear patterns that tell a story about how your teeth function together.\n\nWe take a step back to look at the full system:\n\nIs the crowding purely cosmetic, or is it creating bite stress?\n\nAre there signs of grinding or jaw tension that need to be addressed first?\n\nWill straightening alone solve the problem, or does the bite need correction too?\n\nAre there restorations (crowns, veneers) that factor into the treatment plan?\n\nWhat does your gum health look like before we start moving teeth?\n\nWe won't talk you into Invisalign if something else should come first. And if Invisalign is the right move, we'll plan it with long-term stability in mind, not just a straight smile on the day treatment ends.\n\n\n## Three Reasons Invisalign Works - When It's Planned Right\n\n\n01\n\n\n### No Disruption to Your Life\n\n\nThe aligners come out for meals, brushing, and flossing. You don't change how you eat or how you clean your teeth. Most patients stop noticing the aligners within a few days.\n\n02\n\n\n### Precision Moves, Tracked Over Time\n\n\nEvery aligner set is designed to move specific teeth specific distances. We monitor your progress at regular check-ins and adjust the plan if your teeth respond differently than projected. No case goes on autopilot.\n\n03\n\n\n### A Smile Designed Before Treatment Starts\n\n\nBefore you wear a single aligner, we show you a digital preview of your projected result. You know what you're working toward - you're not hoping it works out. You're watching the plan execute.\n\n\n## Invisalign, Done the Livewell Way\n\n\nHow We Plan Your Case\n\nWe Start With the Diagnosis, Not the Sales Pitch\n\nYour first appointment includes a clinical exam, intraoral scan, and bite analysis. We're not trying to qualify you for a product - we're trying to understand your mouth. That means looking at your gum health, wear patterns, jaw function, and the full picture before recommending anything.\n\nYour Digital Plan Is Built Before You Commit\n\nWe use your 3D scan to map out the full tooth movement sequence. You see the projected before and after on screen. We walk through the plan together, answer your questions, and make sure the goal matches what you actually want.\n\nOne Doctor, Every Appointment, Start to Finish\n\nDr. Chris handles every check-in personally. There's no handoff to an assistant or a hygienist. When your teeth move slower in one area or faster in another, the person who built your plan is the one making the call.\n\nProgress Tracked at Every Stage\n\nWe photograph your teeth at each visit and compare them against your plan. If a tooth isn't tracking correctly, we catch it early - before it throws off the rest of the sequence. Refinements are part of the process, not a sign something went wrong.\n\nFinal Result Documented. Retention Plan Set\n\nWhen treatment is complete, we document your result with professional photos and set you up with retainers designed to hold the position. The work doesn't stop when the last aligner comes out - because that's when most people lose their results.\n\n\n## Hear From Our Patients\n\n\n\"Professional dental care wrapped around hospitality and patient care. Dr. Chris takes your whole person into account when he treats you.\"\n\n-Peter\n\nWatch Now\n\nSEE MORE TESTIMONIALS\n\n\n## Invisalign vs. Braces\n\n\nFeature\n\nInvisalign at Livewell\n\nTraditional Braces\n\nVisibility\n\nNearly invisible\n\nNoticeable metal brackets\n\nRemovable\n\nYes\n\nNo\n\nIn-person monitoring\n\nEvery step, with Dr. Chris\n\nRegular ortho visits\n\nBite correction\n\nYes, when planned correctly\n\nComplex cases\n\nIdeal for\n\nMild to complex cases\n\nVery complex bite issues\n\nBook Your Invisalign Consultation\n\n\n## Start With Clarity, Not Commitment\n\n\nAt Livewell, Invisalign treatment begins with a clear evaluation before any decision is made. You leave your visit understanding what is happening with your teeth, bite, and gum health, and whether clear aligners are the right fit for your goals.\n\nSchedule Your Consultation\n\nCall Us\n\nHow long does Invisalign take?\n\nMild cases can be complete in 6 to 12 months. More involved cases with bite correction typically run 12 to 18 months. We give you a realistic timeline after reviewing your scan - not a number designed to sell you on starting.\n\nDoes Invisalign hurt?\n\nYou'll feel pressure when you switch to a new aligner set, usually for a day or two. Most patients describe it as noticeable but manageable, and it fades quickly as your teeth adjust.\n\nCan I eat and drink normally?\n\nYes. You remove the aligners before eating and drinking anything other than water. That also means your teeth are easier to keep clean during treatment - no food trapped around brackets.\n\nHow many hours a day do I wear them?\n\n20 to 22 hours per day. The more consistently you wear them, the more predictably your teeth move. Skipping wear time is the most common reason cases run longer than planned.\n\nIs Invisalign right for complex cases?\n\nInvisalign can handle cases that once required braces. Whether it's right for your situation depends on your bite, gum health, and bone structure. We'll tell you honestly if braces would serve you better.\n\nWhat happens after I finish treatment?\n\nWe fit you with custom retainers to hold your result. Teeth have memory - without retention, they drift back. We talk through a retainer plan before you finish treatment so there are no surprises.\n\nHow much does Invisalign cost?\n\nInvisalign uses a series of clear aligners to gradually straighten your teeth, and most patients pay $4,000 to $7,000 for treatment. Where you land in that range depends on how much movement your teeth need, how long treatment takes, and how many aligners are required.\n\nIt's also worth asking what's included in your quote, since some cover the consult, scans, refinements, and retainers, while others charge those separately.\n\nGood to know: if your dental plan covers aligners, that can meaningfully lower your out-of-pocket cost.\n\n\n### Frequently Asked Questions\n\n\nContact Us\n\n\n### Reimagine your dental experience\n\n\n\n### address\n\n\n9027 Silverbrook Rd Ste. F\n\nFairfax Station, VA 22039\n\n\n### Contact\n\n\n\n### Hours\n\n\nMon-Tue: 8am-5pm\n\nWed-Thu: 8am-4pm\n\nFri: 8am-1pm\n\n\n### Connect\n\n\nServing Fairfax Station and the Greater Northern Virginia Area\n\nCopyright © TEXT-YEAR Livewell Dental\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms of Service\n\nCookie Policy\n\nHIPAA Disclosure\n\nConsent Preferences",
