            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What happens after I finish treatment?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "We fit you with custom retainers to hold your result. Teeth have memory - without retention, they drift back. We talk through a retainer plan before you finish treatment so there are no surprises."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How much does Invisalign cost?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Invisalign uses a series of clear aligners to gradually straighten your teeth, and most patients pay $4,000 to $7,000 for treatment. Where you land in that range depends on how much movement your teeth need, how long treatment takes, and how many aligners are required. It's also worth asking what's included in your quote, since some cover the consult, scans, refinements, and retainers, while others charge those separately. Good to know: if your dental plan covers aligners, that can meaningfully lower your out-of-pocket cost."
